  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Accordinq to Rydberg&#39;s equation</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>RZ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>where,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo></math> wave number</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo></math> wavelength</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo></math> Rydberg constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>109677</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>=</mo></math> atomic number</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo></math> lower energy state</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></msub><mo>=</mo></math> higher energy state.</p><p>i.e. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi></mfrac><mo>&#8733;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>Thus, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mfenced><msup><mi>He</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mfenced></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><msup><mi>He</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>To find <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mfenced><msup><mi>He</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>?</mo></math></p><p>Given, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>91</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mfenced><mi>He</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mfenced><msup><mi>He</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>91</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math></p>",
